0..77 Comment "// A typed evaluator indexes each expression by the object type of its value."
78..80 Comment "//"
81..157 Comment "// The evaluator then returns the meaning of that type. No check at run time"
158..213 Comment "// reads a tag. The type of each arm states its result."
214..216 Comment "//"
217..296 Comment "// A case on an expression solves each arm\'s index equation. An arm\'s goal then"
297..377 Comment "// reads the arm\'s own index. A branch of the recursion\'s stage moves along that"
378..457 Comment "// equation by its own transport. The object types form a set. So the transport"
458..486 Comment "// keeps the branch\'s stage."
487..489 Comment "//"
490..556 Comment "// - see: #3483 — refinement by solution, by which `eval` checks"
557..638 Comment "// - see: #3631 — a staged branch keeps its stage across its index equation, by"
639..666 Comment "//   which `evalInt` checks"
667..722 Comment "// - see: #3481 — the spike that wrote these programs"
